.superpowers/

# tool caches
.km/

# design canvas working files (the seeded payload is 2.2MB of editor code)
.design/

# Session-local state, by the `.local.` convention the tools that write it use.
# NOT all of .claude/ — that legitimately holds committed project config (agents,
# settings). Only the per-session scratch, which is one session's loop counter and
# has no meaning to anyone who checks the repo out.
.claude/*.local.*

# runs/splits.jsonl is DERIVED — `node scripts/split-ledger.mjs --ingest <verdict.json>` regenerates
# it from the committed verdicts, one command per run — and a derived record stored beside its
# source is the shape this repository recomputes rather than trusts. 86d442a committed it while
# its own README said not to; this line is what stops the next `git add`.
runs/splits.jsonl

# Artifacts written into the working tree BY A LIVE RUN, not by anyone editing this repo.
# Critics hold browser tools and write screenshots, snapshots and console logs to relative
# paths, which land in whatever directory the run was launched from. On 2026-09-02 a
# `git add -A` during a live run swept ~250 of them into a commit alongside a five-file
# source change. They are outputs of a measurement, not part of the instrument.
.playwright-mcp/
# ROOT-LEVEL image and log droppings only. Critics choose their own filenames — the
# 2026-09-02 run wrote doc1-start.png, A-after-harddrop.png, B-stack1.png and 70 more — so a
# name-pattern list cannot hold. Anchored to the root with a leading slash because the
# repo's REAL images are committed evidence under docs/runs/**, and a bare *.png would
# ignore those too: 13 tracked images live there and none at the root.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.log
